! SHIFT CHANGE — the identity watch (handed 2026-09-07)

Triage form, as the prior watch taught: each entry names ''what stands'', ''what it blocks'', and
''the one measurement that settles it''. This watch closed ALL FOUR of the founding watch's owed
rulings and emptied its wiring census; what follows is the ground a fresh Lares needs before touching
identity, recovery, the KEL, the ceremonies, or the ordering of any of it.

!! Ground measured at handoff (2026-09-07)

* ''The four rulings stand CLOSED'' — the veil (per-handle off the VESSEL seed, `deriveDyadVeil`; both ceremony sites mint the dyad slot) · recovery (LAYERED — identity-classes#the-two-forks carries the ruling whole) · seat-adoption (a join grants a seat under the joiner's OWN key; the code already lived it) · the nym's chain (ruled, UNBUILT — the register red carries it).
* ''Two LAWS above the code'' — the ALPHA LINE (no back-compatibility needed until a phone-class vessel joins a PersonaGroup with human eyes on it AND the docker mesh runs green; pre-ruling docs RE-FOUND) and the REGISTRY FILTER (`api/pono/registry-filter` — compiled-about at ANY scope rejects the fork; carriage passes; it ate two drafts on its first day).
* ''The KEL changed bytes TWICE'' (armed inception · rolling commitment) — every prefix re-derives; rehearsal vessels re-found. TWO more grammar changes stand queued and MUST land as ONE settlement (see the lattice below).
* ''Wired this watch:'' the crossing gate prices direction (outward REFUSES, fail-closed, until a cabal quorum surface exists) · `vesselDyads` reads at every vessel's boot through ONE mesh door (node + browser speak the same `[dyad]` line) · the guardian card split into TWO objects (share ⊥ registration, own confirm domains) · `lares nexus seal grow` (the crossing-record ceremony: open · bind · sign · witness · seal).
* ''Register:'' 26 declared reds · 0 ever greened by accident. The mesh scenarios ALL STOOD, one declared GAP: ''realm standing does not cross operators''.
* ''Suites at close:'' lares-cli 225 · keyhive 41+ · full witness family untouched-green; the parallel watches (`@hearth` grammar · `@crossroads` corpus/panel) committed all night interleaved — `git status` before believing any red remains the first law of this tree.

!! THE LATTICE — grounds before wins (operator lens, 2026-09-07)

Rank by ''what inherits shape from what'', never by confidence-of-the-next-wire. The standing order:

# ''G0 — the canon lands'' (THIS gesture: identity-classes fork+axis closed · persona-circle carries the split word "veil" + the declared roster red · `registry-filter` law meme · this block).
# ''G1 — the identity substrate:'' the VEIL-BORN GROUP. Blocks: the admit payload's final shape, the fleet, both humans' real foundings. ''LANDED (2026-09-08) — the founder-side arc stands whole:'' the founding mints a VEIL TAG (persisted in the daemon doc), derives the creator-veil off the vessel seed, and ''the veil-keyed identity CREATES both WHO-plane sentinels'' — the raw vessel Individual holds no grade anywhere, and the byte-law is witnessed at ceremony grain (''no carried event spells the raw vessel key'', `veil-born-group.test.ts`). The runtime stands ''both identities'' (`operator-daemon-behavior`: the veil boots beside the vessel from the persisted tag) and every vessel-bag→face delegation walks ''ONE ROAD'' (`delegateToFaceViaVeil`: vessel→veil admin edge · veil ingests + adopts · veil seats the bag under the group) — the boot's bag caps, the wiki bindings, the face-join re-grants, and `packPersonaCrossing`'s two-handed seat all ride it. The joinee reads shared content end-to-end (`bind-under-handle` green). ''The JOINEE leg LANDED (same day):'' the joinee derives its veil from the CARRIED group doc id, a veil-keyed card seats and READS (the group's material keys to the seated card's prekeys), the apply persists the doc id AS the veil tag (one boot rule stands either veil), and ''both identities' archives survive restarts'' (`veil-archive.bin` beside the vessel's, witnessed across two live boots). ''Remaining on this road:'' the leaf's summons builder presents the veil card when the leaf wire lands (G5) · the bag-plane creator-cleartext stands as its earlier declared concern · the one-road helper's per-call cost stays unmeasured before G4 multiplies callers. Probes that shaped it: self-eviction REFUSED · any-grade-is-roster · carriage-≠-materialization · the coparent door (upstream pothole). ''Three more doors probed (g1-scope.probe.test.ts):'' READ-GRADE members ride the CGKA too — ANY access is roster membership, no sub-roster grade exists (second confirmation, different angle) · CARRIAGE alone does not materialize a doc — a boot must STAND the veil identity, never merely replay its events (`daemonSeesDoc: false` after a 7-event ingest) · the COPARENT-at-birth door is UNMEASURABLE from JS (the slim binding's Peer marshaling throws an unhandled `__wasm_refgen_toJsPeer` error — an upstream pothole for the donation ledger, beside alpha.8's "Redelagation" spelling) · and ''THE BYTES NAMED THE TRUE SURFACE'' (`host-enumeration-surface.probe.test.ts`): ''the CREATOR's identifier rides every carried event in CLEARTEXT'' — greppable by any host with no keys — while an admitted member's id stayed out of the bystander stream. The byte-level cross-group correlator is the EVENT LOG a carrier holds, not the CGKA roster a member reads; the veil-born design covers it exactly (the veil becomes the creator), which upgrades G1 from privacy-hygiene to byte-measured necessity. The declared red + measured cure ride in `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/veil-on-the-roster.test.ts`.
# ''G2 — the KEL grammar freezes WHOLE. Both gates ANSWERED in prose (2026-09-08, identity-classes):'' the HARDENING RULE stands walked (kapae-reversible provisional authority · veto out-competes causally always · observer-local hardening by silence-across-K-local-epochs · contest-keyed board `{prefix}/{seq}/{eventCid}`, veto-beats-provisional fold) and the GRAMMAR FIT ruled the handle-KEL a SIBLING grammar (own domain, ATTESTATION + terminal BURN kinds, owner-binding at inception — G3 builds it on frozen primitives, no bytes-change). ''THE SETTLEMENT LANDED (same day) — THE GRAMMAR IS FROZEN:'' the provisional marker + the veto kind took the persona-KEL's LAST bytes-change under this alpha (`mintVeto` · `foldPersonaContests` · `headOpKey`'s provisional restraint · the board's contest keying with the veto-beats-provisional fold). All four walked clauses stand witnessed (`provisional-veto.test.ts`): a provisional confers only kapae-reversible authority · a late veto kills a hardened provisional AND its descendants · the contest survives the board un-collapsed · an idle observer's patience is the resting state. Rite green, breath green on the rebuilt binary. From here the KEL changes only by a NEW alpha's word.
# ''G3 — the Face's spine. LIFT 1 LANDED (2026-09-09, `5239399f9`):'' the handle-card's bare-key `nym` retired onto the handle-KEL — `nym` now names the KEL PREFIX (stable across rotate/graft/burn), the card carries its CHAIN signed by the current head, and `verifyHandleCard` gained a TIER axis (Tier-1 self-contained ⊥ Tier-2 owner-head-checked, so a self-contained pass never masquerades as board-checked; rejections chain-invalid·nym-mismatch·burned·owner-head-refused). QR ceiling NAMED (`QR_CARRIAGE_MAX_EVENTS=2`, past it paste/file). On-disk: `HandleBookSnapshot` v2 — a pre-KEL bare-key snapshot DROPS on load (versioned reset, re-TOFU from announces — never the silent catch→new wipe); the lossy old→new reconstruction stands as a declared skip (a bare key is not a chain). ''REMAINING: LIFT 2 (the antigen ban-`nym` + its 64-hex gates → the persona-KEL pin-move, a separate plane) UNTOUCHED by design.'' ✓ ''Joint RESOLVED (owner-model ruling, 2026-09-09):'' the personal face is PERSONA-ANCHORED, not self-owned. The contact-read found ONE owner model, not two — `mintHandleInception` is provably sugar over `mintHandleInceptionSet([owner],1,…)`, so 1-of-1 and k-of-n share one structure. The whole joint was one argument `mintPersonaGlamour` passed: the handle key owning ITSELF (foreclosing recovery — a self-owned member resolves to no persona head). Enacted: `mintPersonaGlamour`/`publishPersonaGlamour` now take `ownerPersonaKelPrefix` and seat the OWNING persona-KEL prefix as the sole owner member; a lost presentation key recovers THROUGH the persona (the owner authorizes a rotation). Red-first (`persona-glamour-anchored.test.ts` 2/2), green across mesh/node/browser. The deliberately-standalone sovereign-handle class stays a NAMED, un-foreclosed door (operator's "pono" left it open, unbuilt). ✓ ''THE GLAMOUR SINK LANDED (2026-09-09): `lares handle publish`'' — the FIRST production caller of `publishPersonaGlamour`, the publicly published "here I am" note (a Handle, operator's pet-name). The scout had found source ✓ (personaKelPrefix persisted + boot-loaded) + seam ✓ (`whoFaceCap.announce`) + sink ✗ (no caller); this closes the sink on the node surface. `runHandlePublish` (node adapter) opens the store, loads the persona seed + prefix, resolves the deterministic WHO board (nexusPubkey = vessel key), and mints+announces; the testable core `publishHandleFromDaemonDoc` reads the prefix and ''FAILS CLOSED when it is absent'' — a face with no persona to own it never self-owns (`handle-publish.test.ts` 2/2, CLI dispatch smoke-checked on the built bin). ''REMAINING sinks:'' the browser publish surface + the phone/QR summons presenting the veil card (G5). ✓ ''ISOMORPHIC MOVE + VERB FAMILY (2026-09-09):'' the publish orchestration (`publishHandleFromDaemonDoc`) moved from the node command INTO `@lararium/mesh` (`handle-publish.ts`), so a phone-only holder (three phones + a friend's Nexus) runs the same act — the node adapter keeps only the disk shores. And the `lares handle` noun now scaffolds its whole family: `publish` LIVE · `rotate` · `graft` · `burn` · `attest` as honest stubs (recognized, print their shape + the mesh mint that stands + the canon pointer, exit 3). The four deep ahu (esp. TRUE k-of-n graft governance, `handle-kel.test.ts:400`) stay DECLARED — loop back to wire each vessel-side orchestration. Operator ruled the family a SEPARATE CAP from `persona` (a Handle carries a KEL lifecycle + a k-of-n cardinality a single persona cannot host). Vocabulary trued the same turn: the k-of-n object is a ''k-of-n HandleGlamour'', not "the Mu" — that temp pet-name retired across the identity surface (handle-kel · handle-card · identity-classes · field-collision); the foundational Mu concept untouched. Three absent memes now AUTHORED (`fcb14eaeb`: mesh/handle-card · persona-kel · quorum-entry). Prior map (Seam-Reader): ''RULING-4 IS TWO LIFTS, NOT ONE (corrects the prior "one gesture, one vocabulary"):'' the handle-card `nym` (persona-derived veiled key, social plane) and the antigen `nym` (the vessel's keyhive Identifier `slice(-64)`, transport plane) share NOTHING — different key trees, byte-builders, domains; no value crosses; the word `nym` must not weld them. The card gets the new handle-KEL; the antigen shedding-a-ban rides the ALREADY-BUILT persona-KEL pin-move. ''THE VERIFICATION SEAM — TWO TIERS:'' a card carries its FULL handle-KEL chain (head+proof is crypto-IMPOSSIBLE — maximality has no succinct proof under no-global-now) + the owner persona-prefix + a per-rotation owner-head SNAPSHOT bound into the signed core → Tier 1 self-contained, registry-filter ✅ CARRIAGE (the domain-attestation precedent); the persona board is an OPT-IN strict tier (Identity-plane readers only, ✅ lawful), ❌ REJECTED as mandatory (reads board-absence as now, leaks per-Nexus diffusion onto the public plane). `CardVerdict` gains a third axis so Tier-1 never masquerades as Tier-2. ''THE QR CEILING'' caps a self-contained card at ~2 handle-KEL events — a much-rotated Handle is paste/file-carried; name it at design time. Weld: run the `/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/` gate grep FIRST (10 sites reject a `handle-<hex>` prefix silently-and-closed). ''G3 CORE BUILT (2026-09-08, Bone-Wright): `mesh/handle-kel.ts` stands'' — own domain, armed owner-bound inception (the persona AID inside the prefix hash), owner-authorized rotation (injected resolver — the module never imports the persona grammar), TERMINAL burn, attestations as signed statements (no board). The green-light red greened as a live assertion. ''Builder ⊥ Seam-Reader CONVERGED on the two-tier seam'' (independently): structure/burn/owner-binding/attestation verify card-local; rotation FRESHNESS is the only Identity-plane coupling, and only for a rotated Handle (the common never-rotated case verifies card-complete). ''Q1 RULED 2026-09-08 — OPTION C (either hand burns, the record says which):'' a human runs many non-correlating persona-groups, each maybe bound to a public Handle, so BOTH burn-paths stand — a compromised face SELF-burns (seated key, local, card-verifiable) OR the owner buries the name from above (owner op-key, a thief cannot forge); the burn core's `ownerAuthKeyDid` records the hand, `verifyHandleKelFull` checks the owner-burn against the head resolver. Enacted, `handle-kel.test.ts` 12/12. ''Q2 = PRINCESS BRIDE LAW — DISSOLVED BY THE k-of-n HANDLEGLAMOUR (operator, 2026-09-08) AND ENACTED:'' a Handle and a cabal-realm carry ONE pattern integrity — a valid presentation whose human-cardinality stays unknowable — so the Dread Pirate Roberts is a Handle whose PRESENTING QUORUM grafts members, never a succession mechanism. Enacted (`8cf6a0cbb`): the owner-binding generalized from a single prefix to an owner-SET (genesis digest in the prefix = anti-swap · rolling current-set per event), 1-of-1 the degenerate personal face, presentation by any current member, succession = a GRAFT rolling the set (authorized by one member — DPR's case; true k-of-n graft governance DECLARED as a skipped red). Answers both kept kue (civic cryptographic-continuity · crew-resurrection). Canon: identity-classes#the-handle-chain "the k-of-n HandleGlamour". The #cede-mechanism hoike is SUPERSEDED — the fork dissolved. ''Deeper reach flagged, unbuilt:'' the presenting cabal MAY be the recovery cabal (one quorum, both roles) — a simplification larger than this build scoped. ''FIELD COLLISION (2026-09-08, `api/pono/field-collision`):'' SPKI/SDSI + KERI vindicate the ontology twice-over; the #1-exposure (CONIKS equivocation-detection) DISSOLVED at primary source (it gossips COMPACT commitments per-reader — that IS carriage; the registry filter survives). ''Two OWED capabilities surfaced:'' (1) WATCHERS — HOME NAMED, SUBSTRATE CHECKED (2026-09-08, Meme-Warden): the watcher's home is the Meshpalace SENSORIUM (ITC/getHeads gossip), and it ''does NOT stand in code'' — the `mesh-palace.ts` FLOW-map (routing chart) exists but is the MAP not the sensorium. The primitives stand (`itc.ts`, `detectDuplicity`, the veto/fold that CONSUMES duplicity in-chain); what's missing is the layer that GOSSIPS head-sightings to surface inconsistency across the mesh. ''Watchers await a WHOLE PALACE (the federation-last sensorium), not a wire'' — the earlier 'wire onto designed ground' overstated it. Also authored (`fcb14eaeb`): the three absent memes `mesh/handle-card`, `mesh/persona-kel`, `mesh/quorum-entry`, grounded in the built code. (2) The φ-accrual hardening must BOUND its silence-wait (TUF: silence is ambiguous — an attacker freezes a victim by withholding). ''Canon made honest (2026-09-08):'' the ITC 'in-production' claim STRUCK at source (mechanism verified, deployment was a search-summary confabulation — the ward caught it); Deseriis's vocabulary folded (1-of-1 = multiple-use name · k-of-n = collective pseudonym); the beneficial-ownership doctrine firmed (KYC lives ENTIRELY at the web2 bridge, never sovereign carriage — declared red `contractPlaneKycAtBridge`). ''Two standing tensions, operator-aware:'' moderation ("ban the person" lost to hidden cardinality — answered by capability-propagation, honestly partial) and beneficial-ownership law (the KYC record lives at the web2 bridge, behind the island wall, never in sovereign carriage). ''Owed:'' the NYM RETIREMENT wiring (run the `/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/` gate grep first) · the three cited memes `mesh/handle-card` · `mesh/persona-kel` · `mesh/quorum-entry` now AUTHORED (`fcb14eaeb`) · the resolver-freshness contract (a caller wiring "was ever a head" reopens the superseded-key hole — the resolver MUST answer "current unsuperseded un-vetoed head").
# ''G4 — the gatherings.'' MEASURED (2026-09-08, Cost-Warden): ''(a) the one-road cost scales SUPERLINEAR'' — 2.5–2.7× across an N=16 batch, stable over 3 runs, because `eventsForPeer` re-ships the veil's whole history per call; so ''fleet-gather MUST BATCH'' (per-dyad road calls compound quadratically at fleet width — the gradient decides, not the ~20ms base; probe: `keyhive/tests/one-road-cost.probe.test.ts`, reds on regression). ''(b) the realm-crossing GAP is a WIRE, ruling already landed'' — B's feed slot lands in B's DAEMON bag (`realm-feed` writes `DAEMON_BAG_ID`; the cross-operator class never grants a private-own plane), so A structurally cannot see B's face; the cure points the realm verbs' store at `CabalRealm.substrateUrl` (the shared CRDT) and requires the seal on foreign slots — `realmFeedPrefix` + `verifyRealmFeedSlot` already stand for it. Then: fleet-gather (batched) · the petname-switcher unification (+ the pet-name book's ritual surface) · the cabal quorum surface (the outward crossing's lawful yes) · the browser tier door · the compartment-collector check.
# ''G5 — the humans arrive on settled ground:'' Freyja's live crossing (the verb stands; the pending-image custody question resolves before a rite spans days), then the phone (QR wire · the breath on glass) — the alpha exit walked LAST, its scenarios grown one-per-phase along the way.

!! Instruments this watch measured (carry them)

* ''Know what your import resolves to'' — `@lararium/mesh` reads SRC under node's vitest aliases and DIST under lares-cli's; the same symbol "missing" means a stale dist, not absent code. Bit twice.
* ''A unit fake without the live shape hides the defect'' — `coerceDyad` rebuilt every slot from its edge and every unit test stayed green; only the read-meets-mint vector over a REAL ceremony doc caught it.
* ''The other writer is the operator'' (again) — a broad parallel commit carried this watch's dirty gate; a lone red traced to their committed spelling migration. Report, never grab.
* ''A ruling's own vocabulary is the deliverable'' — coined shorthand ("back-compass") drifted from the ruled words and needed truing; canon carries the OPERATOR'S words.

