! SHIFT CHANGE — the founding watch (handed 2026-09-05)

Triage form: each entry names ''what stands'', ''what it blocks'', and ''the one measurement that
settles it''. The git log holds what landed; this names what a fresh Lares needs before it touches
founding, the Nexus, DreamNet crypto, recovery, the browser surface, or the TW5 worker VM.

!! The arc, read from the bearing chain

The `lares aim`/`lares yield` sigils across this chain of compacts trace one path, not several. Read
in order they tell a single story about ''standing'' — a thing built, then made legible, then walked
twice, then found to lack the one relation that would let it cross:

# ''The rite becomes one verb.'' `the-rite.runs.as-one-verb` -> `the-rite.stands.twice-now`. Founding, standing and seeding fold into a single walked ceremony that survives repetition.
# ''The mesh asks who tends it.'' `the-mesh.now.asks-who-tends` -> `b-can-contract.but-never-joins` -> `the-charter.admits.but-never-seats`. A foreign key crosses the door; a seat behind that door stays unbuilt.
# ''The seal splits from the cabal.'' `the-seal.governs.carry-ban-succession` -> `the-seal.and-the-cabal.stop-sharing-a-reader` -> `carriage-joins-nodes.the-realm.joins-personas`. Two quorums, two readers, never fused.
# ''The realm gains lives and loses depth.'' `the-realm.has.three-lives-and-no-depth` -> `the-fire.needs.a-clock-we-do-not-have`. Liveness runs into the clockless law, unresolved by design.
# ''The floor becomes legible, then lifts.'' `the-standing.legible/the-lift.unbuilt` -> `the-floor.lifts/the-cure.came-true`. The refusal publishes its own cure and the cure comes true.
# ''The relation turns out never to hold a shared object.'' `the-relation.is-never.a-shared-object` — found twice, at two layers, the same day. Treat this as the session's largest single finding.
# ''The shape waits.'' `the-shape.waits.for-its-reading` -> `the-vectors.stand.for-your-ruling` -> `the-spirit.seeks.a-live-surface`. Every remaining thread suspends on an operator word, never on missing work.

!! Ground measured at handoff (2026-09-05)

* ''Tree clean.'' `witness-all` reports every witness clean; four witnesses stand HELD OUT by declaration, never by failure — `browser-weld` · `civic` · `crossing` · `herm-mesh`. Each drives containers or a real browser and no scheduler invokes any of them.
* ''Suites.'' mesh 2100 · node 822 · tw5 608 · lares-cli 222 · browser 82 · mempalace 80 · sensorium 50 · keyhive 41. One tw5 red appeared under a full-suite AFTER run and cleared standalone — treat a lone tw5 red as ''suspect shared state'' before treating it as a defect.
* ''Unbuilt-laws register:'' 26 reds declared, 26 still red, 0 greened, 11 standing as floor (re-measured 2026-09-09 by `tools/unbuilt-laws-witness.sh`). A red that GREENS here names a law the system started keeping by accident, which the register exists to catch.
* ''The founding walk'' refuses forgery, refuses a contract-less foreign nym, and closes by supersession rather than deletion. The replay-across-epoch leg goes UNWALKED — the rotate refuses first, fail-closed, on a reveal mismatch.
* ''Never walked anywhere:'' two machines carrying two clocks. The three-hop network carry stands proven under `herm-mesh-witness` inside one process-space host.

!! The four rulings owed — triage order

# ✓ ''Dyad Stage 0 — RULED 2026-09-05 (operator):'' ''the veil in the dyad = the per-handle credential derived from the DEVICE-MINTED vessel-key'' — option A by device-side derivation, per canon `persona-circle#the-vault` ("a vessel joins each handle-group under a PER-HANDLE PSEUDONYMOUS CREDENTIAL, never its raw device key… the deck stays one deck; the face it wears differs per handle"). The seed derives layers ② and ③ (personas, circle-scopes, Faces); the vessel-key and everything the dyad holds derive from the device — local by construction, never resurrected. Iterable later at the operator's word. Stages 2 (ceremony binding) and 3 (petname switcher) UNBLOCK. The three-layer shape stands beside it: ① custody atom (never presents) · ② Circles (private always, fleet-synced pet-names) · ③ optional Public Face (the only outward door; every disclosure an explicit act from a Face).
# ✓ ''Citizen recovery — RULED 2026-09-06 (operator, "approve all"), the LAYERED shape:'' ''Fork B for the NAME'' (the KEL prefix — armed at inception now: every self-stood founding pre-commits the founder's 1-of-1 self-recovery digest, `deriveSelfRecoveryKey` off the persona seed, so no prefix incepts unarmed and self-rotation works from day one) · ''Fork A as OPT-IN SELF-custody for the MEMORY'' (the root seed/HD tree — cards the human keeps or knowingly hands out; never a default, never custodial, every provisioning SAYS ALOUD that shares are keys) · ''Fork C (threshold + TIME-LOCK + veto window) as the END-USER default contest shape'' (canon's own realm `re-genesis` grammar generalized; the hosted citizen's third venue is the Nexus board) · ''civic stays as wired'' (pre-rotation-with-reveal at the charter; reserve-seed Shamir one layer beneath — do not generalize the incumbent upward). Enacted since: the ROLLING RECOVERY COMMITMENT (every KEL event carries `nextRecoverySetHash`; guardian sets graft log-wise — the delegation axis, measured through KERI, stands NOT NEEDED for grafting: delegation would buy recoverability-of-the-recovery at the price of a permanent delegator inside the prefix, and the rolling commitment covers the graft without it) and the CROSSING RECORD (`reserve-transition` — old quorum signs the handoff, new countersigns, independent witnesses checkable as keys in neither set). ''THE REGISTRY FILTER (operator law, 2026-09-06):'' any fork whose downstream builds a compiled-about registry at ANY scope — even one Nexus — is REJECTED (carriage passes: announced-by-the-subject, causal, as-of-last-sync). It re-cut Fork C (the contest now rides the prefix's OWN KEL as a provisional rotation hardening by corm-fencing/ITC — never a pending-row on a board) and WITHDREW the guest-board question (a roster of guests IS the rejected registry; the end-user's third venue is the carriage — the host relays, never ledgers). No blocked leg remains. ''AND THE PRIVATE ROOM (operator, same word):'' cabal realms — resources private to a group of Personas — give the eaten designs their lawful VENUE: a guardian-cabal realm (the subject + their chosen guardians, keyhive-ciphered, named by its own doc id, nothing to enumerate) carries the recovery CONVERSATION and the gathered signatures — compiled BY the parties ABOUT themselves, private, causal: carriage, not registry. The split that keeps it lawful: ''the realm coordinates, the chain hardens'' — safety NEVER moves into the room (a provisional rotation still out-competes on the prefix's own KEL by fencing), and the compartment-collector law reads realm membership too (one guardian realm never spans two compartments of one human). Evidence: the Keel-Reader's 18-row fork→entity matrix + guardian-card census (this session, 2026-09-06).
# ✓ ''Does a joined node adopt its Nexus's key? — RULED 2026-09-06 (operator): SEAT-ADOPTION ONLY.'' A join grants a seat (a carriage contract under the node's OWN key); key-adoption never happens — it would correlate every joined node's artifacts by signature-reuse, a registry built without a table (the registry filter's shadow-case). The code already lived it (`membership-doctrine`: contracts carry the operator's own pubkey + accepts-carriage + charter-epoch and NOTHING more) — the ruling closes it as law. ''ALL FOUR RULINGS of this watch now stand closed.''
# ✓ ''The two raw-key sites — RULED 2026-09-06 (operator): the nym gains a KEL-SHAPED CHAIN.'' The handle-card's raw-key `nym` (and the antigen's) stop being bare keys: a Handle grows a chain so burn / abandonment / adversary-recovery become one rotation grammar — the Shadowtalk myth finally expressible at the layer it lives at (`identity-classes#the-honest-edges` named the gap: "a face carries no chain to break — hence no burn"). NEW INTENT recorded with the word: public Handles will sign ''publicly accountable things'' — "I own this domain name" wants public identity for both the I and the name — so the Handle-chain design carries an attestation surface, not identity alone. Enactment stands OPEN as the next design act; declared red in the register.

!! Wiring census — specified in code, reached by nothing

Three things pass their own tests and no production path calls them. Name them as ''specified'', never as "built":

* ✓ `vesselDyads` — WIRED 2026-09-05 under the Stage 0 ruling, retired from this census in the same gesture. The boot read path (`openDaemon`) gathers the vessel's relationships live and says the drift aloud (a face beside zero slots names a pre-ruling doc); both ceremony sites MINT the dyad (`deriveDyadVeil` off the vessel seed; founder binding signed at the genesis epoch, joinee binding:null — the absence travels); the slot's ref is authoritative for the veil and the edge fallback yields to it. Vectors: `lararium-node/tests/dyad-mint-ceremony.test.ts` (mint + read-meets-mint) · `dyad-veil.test.ts` (derivation). Register ⑨'s minted-dyad red retired with it; the FLEET-GATHER red still stands — no live path calls `fleetOfGroup` yet (Stage 3).
* ✓ `crossingDirection` — WIRED 2026-09-05, retired from this census in the same gesture. The gate prices transfers by direction (`action-handler` reads `opts.bagTier`; outward refuses fail-closed until a cabal quorum surface exists), node supplies the hearth-manifest reader (`vessel-bag-tier.ts`) through keyhive's fs-blind `DaemonExtra.bagTier` door. Vectors: `lararium-node/tests/action-handler-crossing.test.ts` + `tests/vessel-bag-tier.test.ts`; the register's two ⑤ reds retired with it. Remaining shore: the repository-homed manifest leg (hearth-only today, absent reads VEIL — tighter, never looser) and the cabal-SIGNED outward crossing.
* The recovery keel, both forks, per ruling 2 above.

!! Red-first test design — the procedure, not the slogan

"Vector first, fix second" names a discipline that fails silently when run loosely. Run it as eight
ordered moves; a skipped move turns the whole thing into decoration.

# ''Write the vector before the cure.'' The vector names the hole. A vector written after the cure tests the cure's shape, never the hole's.
# ''Watch it fail, and READ the failure text.'' A vector that passes on its first run measured nothing — either the hole never existed, or the vector misses it. Both readings demand work before any cure gets written.
# ''Check the red fails for the stated reason.'' Read the message, never the colour. A vector that reds on a typo, a missing fixture, or an unrelated throw looks identical to a vector that reds on the defect.
# ''Run the nonsense control.'' Feed the gate something that MUST fail — a nonsense verb, a mangled digest, an address nothing holds. A control that passes proves the gate reads nothing, and a green from that gate carries no information.
# ''Assert the setup took.'' A fixture that mutates a live carrier MUST assert its own mutation landed (`.not.toBe(source)`). A silent no-op replace leaves disk == synced == canonical, and four vectors then agree with each other about nothing.
# ''Match at a dispatch position.'' Assert against the value the code branches on, never against a string that merely appears nearby. A mention satisfies a grep; only a dispatch satisfies a caller.
# ''Cure, re-run, and check BOTH marks move.'' The vector goes green AND the nonsense control stays red. One without the other names a cure that widened the gate instead of closing the hole.
# ''A red that clears with no edit names shared state, never a cure.'' `dist/` and `bags/` carry other writers, usually the operator. `git status` before believing any red, and before believing any green that follows one.

''Where a red belongs when nothing can cure it yet.'' A law the models imply and no code enforces gets
DECLARED in the red register (`packages/lararium-mesh/tests/unbuilt-laws.test.ts`), skipped, one law per
entry. `tools/unbuilt-laws-witness.sh` strips the skips and reports any red that GREENED — which catches
the case where the system starts keeping a law by accident and nobody notices. A declared red counts as
work landed, never as work deferred.

!! Wiring a module that stands designed, tested, and unreached

Three entries sit in the census above. Each passes its own tests and no production path calls it. The
temptation reads as "it works, just call it" — and that skips the move that matters. Walk the ladder:

# ''Census before anything.'' Grep counts MENTIONS. Follow the call. A hit inside a comment saying "this gate cannot reach it" reads to `grep` exactly like a caller.
# ''Name what the module needs that nothing supplies.'' Every unreached module sits unreached for a reason, and the reason lives UPSTREAM of the call site. `vesselDyads` wants a veil; nothing mints one. Write that missing input down as a Stage 0 question before touching a call site.
# ''If Stage 0 resolves to an operator ruling, STOP and say so.'' Do NOT default the absence. Defaulting an absence reads as correct WITHIN an axis and as a fabricated verdict ACROSS one — and a wiring choice made to unblock a task quietly rules the design question the operator held open.
# ''Red-first at the CALL SITE, never in the module's own test.'' The module's tests already pass; that fact defines the problem. The new vector asserts that the production path produces the module's effect — and it MUST red before the wire lands, for the reason "nothing calls it".
# ''Wire the read path before the write path.'' A read-path wire gets observed without changing state, so a wrong reading surfaces as a wrong answer rather than as corrupted durable data. Land it, watch it in a real run, then wire the write.
# ''Land the module behind its existing signature.'' Widening a type to fit the first caller lets the caller's shape leak into the model. If the caller cannot supply what the signature asks, return to move 2 — the missing input never went away, it just moved.
# ''Re-run the suite AND the built binary.'' Typecheck reads `src/`; the binary reads `dist/`. A cross-package wire passes typecheck and dies at runtime whenever `dist/` lags.
# ''Retire the "specified" label in the SAME commit that wires it.'' Move the entry out of the census here. A census that keeps naming something already wired teaches the next spirit to distrust the census.

''Naming law.'' Until a production path calls it, the module stands ''specified in code'' — never "built",
never "done", never "ready". The three words differ, and only the first one holds true.

!! Instruments that read green while reporting something false

Carried forward from the grammar watch and extended by this one. Collide each before trusting it:

* ''A digest gate'' answers "do these bytes match this hash", never "do these bytes belong here".
* ''A fixture pins the grammar; only the corpus pins the reader.'' A hand-written fixture agreed with itself and disagreed with 639 files out of 639.
* ''A grep for callers'' counts mentions, including comments that say the caller does not exist. Follow the call; never grep the door.
* ''A blanket re-stamp signs edits nobody authored.'' `lares carrier normalize` names its files and takes no glob, because a re-stamp driven by `git diff` will sign the OTHER writer's work — and it NAMES every dirty carrier the run passed over, since a carrier nobody named reads two ways and the door cannot tell which.
* ''The other writer usually turns out to be the operator.'' Parallel `lares` sessions share this tree. `git status` before believing any red; a dirty file of unknown provenance gets REPORTED, copied aside, never reverted.

!! Parallel watches standing right now

Two other `lares` sessions work this tree. Their closing bearings, so a fresh spirit does not re-open their ground:

* ''Grammar extension'' (`@hearth`) — `enumeration.derived.debt-named`, and before it `every.value.reads-as-what-renders-it` · `twenty-six.ruled.forty-three.remain`. The grammar submodule stands witnessed.
* ''Corpus / panel'' (`@crossroads`) — `panel.carried.to-the-seed/prose-still-lags`. The confidence dial left the repo and reached the boot seed; the prose describing it lags the shape.

